<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">26 January in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">8 events that happened on 26 January, from 661 to 1998.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-muljam" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ibn-muljam.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/661">661 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">1,365 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Ibn Muljam attacks Caliph Ali at prayer in Kufa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Kharijite <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-muljam">Ibn Muljam</a> struck the fourth <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/caliphate">caliph</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-ibn-abi-talib">Ali ibn Abi Talib</a>, with a poisoned sword as he prayed in the Great Mosque of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kufa">Kufa</a>. Ali died of his wounds two days later, which ended the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a>.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ali-ibn-abi-talib">Ali ibn Abi Talib</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ibn-muljam">Ibn Muljam</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rashidun-caliphate">Rashidun Caliphate</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1500">1500 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">526 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Vicente Yáñez Pinzón lands on the coast of Brazil</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Spanish navigator, who had captained the Niña under <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/christopher-columbus">Columbus</a>, landed near Cape Santo Agostinho in today's Pernambuco. He arrived three months before Cabral, but <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a> fell within Portugal's sphere.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brazil">Brazil</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1788">1788 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">238 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">First Fleet raises the British flag at Sydney Cove</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Captain <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arthur-phillip">Arthur Phillip</a> established a penal colony at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sydney-cove">Sydney Cove</a> with some 1,300 convicts, marines and officials. The date is marked as <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a> Day, and by many Indigenous Australians as a day of mourning.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/australia">Australia</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1837">1837 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">189 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Michigan becomes the 26th US state</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Michigan joined the Union after giving up the disputed <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a> Strip to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ohio">Ohio</a>, the cause of the bloodless 'Toledo War'. In exchange it received most of the Upper Peninsula.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/toledo">Toledo</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1905">1905 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">121 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Cullinan diamond, the largest ever found, discovered</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Mine manager Frederick <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/well">Wells</a> found a 3,106-carat rough diamond at the Premier Mine near <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pretoria">Pretoria</a>. Cut into nine major stones, it supplied the largest gems in the British Crown Jewels.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1934">1934 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">92 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Germany and Poland sign a non-aggression pact</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hitler's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a> and Piłsudski's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/poland">Poland</a> agreed a ten-year declaration of non-aggression. It loosened Poland's ties with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a>; Hitler renounced it in April 1939 and invaded that September.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1950">1950 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">76 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">India becomes a republic under its new constitution</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/constitution-of-india">Constitution of India</a> came into force and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rajendra-prasad">Rajendra Prasad</a> became the first President, replacing the British monarch as head of state. The day is celebrated as Republic Day.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year"><a href="/years/1998">1998 CE</a> <span class="tih-ago">28 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Bill Clinton denies an affair with Monica Lewinsky</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">At the White House, President Clinton declared he 'did not have sexual relations with that woman'. He later admitted an inappropriate relationship and was impeached by the House in December 1998, then acquitted.</p></div></li></ol>
